# HOM-346: example env for the `graph/` LangGraph project.
#
# Copy to `graph/.env` and fill in. `langgraph dev` and `langgraph up`
# both auto-load `graph/.env` (configured via `graph/langgraph.json`'s
# `"env": ".env"` entry).
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres URI for step-debug resumability (HOM-334 Phase B)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required when running `langgraph up` so thread/interrupt state survives
# Studio process restarts. NOT consumed by `langgraph dev` — its inmem
# runtime serialises to `.langgraph_api/.langgraph_checkpoint.*.pckl` and
# does not honor POSTGRES_URI (verified against langgraph-cli 0.4.24 +
# langgraph-runtime-inmem 0.28.0 on 2026-05-24).
#
# To get a local Postgres on port 5433:
#   docker compose -f graph/docker-compose.yml up -d langgraph-postgres
#
# POSTGRES_URI=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/postgres?sslmode=disable

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# LangSmith API key (required by `langgraph up`)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# `langgraph up` validates a LangSmith API key on every boot (or accepts
# a LANGGRAPH_CLOUD_LICENSE_KEY for offline use). `langgraph dev` does
# not require either. Set this only if you intend to run the postgres-
# backed Studio for multi-session step-debug walkthroughs.
#
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=lsv2_...
# LANGGRAPH_CLOUD_LICENSE_KEY=...
